# ADR-0035: the real Camouflage, cast in human's declare attackers step,
# leaves an effect card whose Event$ DeclareBlocker replacement takes ai's
# blocker declaration's place. No "queue blocks" line: ai is never asked to
# declare. Instead ai (ReplacedPlayer, the declarer) makes one pile per
# attacker from its own creatures -- Devoted Hero alone, then Silvercoat Lion
# alone -- and the piles go to Craw Wurm and Grizzly Bears in the order
# g.rand's shuffle of the attackers gives (CardLists.shuffle,
# CamouflageEffect.java:22). With this seed the Hero's pile lands on the
# Wurm and the Lion's on the Bears: the Hero dies to the Wurm, the Bears and
# the Lion trade. Nobody is unblocked, so ai stays at 20.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 3,4
declareattackers
tapformana human 2 G
castspell human 1
resolvestack
advance
queue cardchoice 5
queue cardchoice 6
declareblockers
advance
advance
combatdamage
# On through the state-based-action check that moves the lethally damaged
# creatures to their graveyards, to cleanup, where the "this turn" effect
# card leaves the Command zone and the Wurm's damage wears off.
advance
advance
advance
advance
